---
title: SEVEN_SEGMENT - HT1621 driver mode
---
%% Pins from the HT1621 example in Peripherals/SEVEN_SEGMENT/README.md,
%% remapped onto free pins from project.ioc.
%% The driver also supports direct GPIO multiplexing, but that costs 8 segment
%% pins plus one per digit - more than the 22 free pins allow for 4+ digits,
%% so the HT1621 path is the practical one on this board.
%% The HT1621 is a 3-wire bit-banged bus, not real SPI.
%% It refreshes the display itself, so the CPU is not tied up multiplexing.
flowchart LR
    subgraph MCU["STM32F429I-DISC1"]
        CS["PC11 - CS"]
        WR["PC12 - WR clock"]
        DAT["PC13 - DATA"]
        V33["3V3"]
        GND["GND"]
    end

    subgraph HT["HT1621 module"]
        hCS["CS"]
        hWR["WR"]
        hDAT["DATA"]
        hV["VDD 3.3-5 V"]
        hG["GND"]
    end

    subgraph DISP["Multi-digit 7-segment LCD"]
        SEGS["Segments a b c d e f g dp"]
        DIGS["Digit commons"]
    end

    CS --> hCS
    WR --> hWR
    DAT --> hDAT
    V33 --- hV
    GND --- hG
    hDAT -.->|"SEG0..SEG31"| SEGS
    hDAT -.->|"COM0..COM3"| DIGS
